.TH "TEMPORAL.PLAINMONTHDAY.PLAINMONTHDAY" "3JS" "September 18, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Temporal.PlainMonthDay.PlainMonthDay \- Temporal.PlainMonthDay()
constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]Temporal.PlainMonthDay()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates
\f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay\f[R] objects.
.PP
This constructor allows you to create instances by directly supplying
the underlying data.
Like all other \f[CR]Temporal\f[R] classes, you should usually construct
\f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay\f[R] objects using the
\f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay.from()\f[R] static method, which can handle
a variety of input types.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new Temporal.PlainMonthDay(month, day)
new Temporal.PlainMonthDay(month, day, calendar)
new Temporal.PlainMonthDay(month, day, calendar, referenceYear)
.EE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] \f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay()\f[R] can only be
constructed with \f[CR]new\f[R].
Attempting to call it without \f[CR]new\f[R] throws a
\f[CR]TypeError\f[R].
.RE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Warning:\f[R] Avoid using the \f[CR]calendar\f[R] and
\f[CR]referenceYear\f[R] parameters, because \f[CR]equals()\f[R] will
consider the reference year for equality, causing two equivalent
month\-days to be considered different if they have different reference
years.
To create a \f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay\f[R] object with a non\-ISO
calendar, use the \f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay.from()\f[R] static
method.
.RE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]month\f[R]
A number, truncated to an integer, representing the month in the ISO
calendar system.
.TP
\f[B]day\f[R]
A number, truncated to an integer, representing the day of the month in
the ISO calendar system.
.TP
\f[B]calendar\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string representing the calendar to use.
See \f[CR]Intl.supportedValuesOf()\f[R] for a list of commonly supported
calendar types.
Defaults to \f[CR]\(dqiso8601\(dq\f[R].
Note that irrespective of the \f[CR]calendar\f[R], the
\f[CR]referenceYear\f[R], \f[CR]month\f[R], and \f[CR]day\f[R] must be
in the ISO 8601 calendar system.
.TP
\f[B]referenceYear\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A number, truncated to an integer, representing the year in the ISO
calendar system.
Defaults to \f[CR]1972\f[R].
The same ISO month\-day can represent different dates in different years
with non\-ISO calendars.
For example, the days 2021\-07\-01 and 1972\-07\-01 may fall on
different month\-days in a non\-Gregorian calendar, and just specifying
\(lq07\-01\(rq is insufficient to unambiguously determine a month\-day
in the target calendar.
Therefore, you virtually always want to specify a
\f[CR]referenceYear\f[R] when using a non\-ISO calendar.
.SS Return value
A new \f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay\f[R] object, representing the
month\-day of the date specified by \f[CR]referenceYear\f[R],
\f[CR]month\f[R], \f[CR]day\f[R] (in the ISO calendar), interpreted in
the calendar system specified by \f[CR]calendar\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Thrown if \f[CR]calendar\f[R] is not a string or \f[CR]undefined\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]RangeError\f[R]
Thrown in one of the following cases:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]referenceYear\f[R], \f[CR]month\f[R], or \f[CR]day\f[R] is not a
finite number.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]referenceYear\f[R], \f[CR]month\f[R], and \f[CR]day\f[R]
combination does not represent a valid date in the ISO calendar system,
or is not in the representable range, which is ±(10\(ha8 + 1) days, or
about ±273,972.6 years, from the Unix epoch.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]calendar\f[R] is not a valid calendar identifier.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using Temporal.PlainMonthDay()
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] md = \f[B]new\f[R] Temporal.PlainMonthDay(7, 1);
console.log(md.toString()); \f[I]// 07\-01\f[R]

\f[B]const\f[R] md2 = \f[B]new\f[R] Temporal.PlainMonthDay(7, 1, \(dqchinese\(dq);
console.log(md2.toString()); \f[I]// 1972\-07\-01[u\-ca=chinese]\f[R]

\f[B]const\f[R] md3 = \f[B]new\f[R] Temporal.PlainMonthDay(7, 1, \(dqchinese\(dq, 2021);
console.log(md3.toString()); \f[I]// 2021\-07\-01[u\-ca=chinese]\f[R]
.EE
.SS Improper usage
You should avoid using the \f[CR]calendar\f[R] and
\f[CR]referenceYear\f[R] parameters, unless you know that the
\f[CR]referenceYear\f[R] is the canonical reference year that would be
selected by \f[CR]Temporal.PlainMonthDay.from()\f[R] for the same
month\-day.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] md = \f[B]new\f[R] Temporal.PlainMonthDay(7, 1, \(dqchinese\(dq, 2021);
\f[B]const\f[R] md2 = Temporal.PlainMonthDay.from(\(dq2021\-07\-01[u\-ca=chinese]\(dq);
console.log(md.equals(md2)); \f[I]// false\f[R]
console.log(md.toString()); \f[I]// 2021\-07\-01[u\-ca=chinese]\f[R]
console.log(md2.toString()); \f[I]// 1972\-07\-02[u\-ca=chinese]\f[R]
.EE
